Implementation Strategy and Modernization Roadmap
To successfully implement these workflow optimizations, enterprises should follow the principle of "optimize processes first, automate second". Investing heavily in advanced ERP platforms without clarifying underlying accounting procedures will only digitalize existing bottlenecks and increase employee friction.   

Initially, a thorough audit of the current software ecosystem and physical document flow must be carried out to identify manual overhead. Following this, the finance leadership team must establish updated SOPs and clear boundaries of responsibility for sub-ledger and general accountants within a collaborative workspace.   

Technologically, the business should migrate from fragmented accounting software to an integrated ERP system that supports Event-Driven Architecture and real-time syncing. Strict multi-tenant security, API-first integrations (e.g., e-invoicing and corporate banking), and AI OCR modules must be deployed to eliminate manual entry.   

Finally, a structured change-management and training program should be introduced. Sub-ledger accountants must transition from manual data entry operators to data controllers, while general accountants must be trained in data analytics and automated closing tools. In light of strict regulatory frameworks like Law No. 108/2025/QH15, achieving real-time digital integration is no longer a luxury, but a core compliance standard for modern enterprises.   

